# Changelog updates

When you add, change, or remove user-facing behavior (API, client features, crypto, migrations that affect clients, tooling users rely on), update [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) in the same change set.

## Conventions (from CHANGELOG.md)

- On branches not yet merged to `main`, put entries under **`## [NEXT RELEASE]`**.
- Follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/): use `### Added` / `### Changed` / `### Fixed` / `### Removed` as needed.
- Group bullets under existing subsections when they fit: **Server**, **Client**, **Tooling & deployment**.
- Keep the short intro line under `NEXT RELEASE` accurate if the product posture changed (e.g. encryption status).
- Do not invent a semver release heading until a release is cut on `main`.

## When arranging / committing feature work

Include the CHANGELOG update in the docs commit (or the feature commit if there is no separate docs commit). Do not leave notable shipped work undocumented in CHANGELOG.
